Draw the circle
To draw a circle, we use the cv2.circle() function of the OpenCV library. This function requires five parameters, which are listed below:

img is the image on which we’ll draw the circle.
center is the center point of the circle around which the circle will be drawn. We can use any image editing tool to find the center of the football.
radius is the radius of the circle.
redColor adds red color to the circle. It can be changed to another color with a different color code. We’ll learn about this in detail in the next chapter.
circleThickness is the thickness of the circle.

