Draw the rectangle
To draw a rectangle, we use the cv2.rectangle() function of the OpenCV library. This function requires five parameters, which are listed below:

img is the image on which we’ll draw the rectangle.
leftTopCorner is the top left corner point of the image where we want to draw the rectangle.
rightBottomCorner is the bottom right corner point of the image where we want to draw the rectangle.
yellowColor adds yellow color to the rectangle. It can be changed to another color with a different color code. We’ll learn about this in detail in the next chapter.
rectangleThickness is the thickness of the rectangle.

