Draw a line
To draw a line, we use the cv2.line() function of the OpenCV library. This function requires five parameters, which are listed below:

img is the image on which we’ll draw the line.
startPoint is the starting point of the line. In this example, it is the left top corner of the image.
endPoint is the ending point of the line. In this example, it is the bottom right corner of the image.
whiteColor adds white color to the line. It can be changed to another color with a different color code. We’ll learn about this in detail in the next chapter.
lineThickness is the thickness of the line.

